jobResponsibilities:
The Private & Shared Mobility Division oversees the development of private transport policies, encompassing vehicles, roads, and active mobility, and is also responsible for the development of strategies to prepare the MOT Family for future mobility challenges and opportunities, particularly in the areas of sustainability, research and development and inter-modal connectivity. 

As part of the Private Mobility team, you are expected to work together with other government agencies to:
• Develop and review private mobility strategies and policies, such as on the Certificate of Entitlement;
• Develop measures to contribute to the transport sector’s move towards sustainability, including measures to scale up electric vehicle adoption;
• Study trends that may impact the future of transport and develop proposals to enable Singapore to stay ahead of these trends; and
• Engage international and local thought leaders from both the private and public sectors, as well as help spur industry development efforts.

Your key responsibilities include:

•	Planning and managing CAD’s budget;
•	Providing guidance to CAD’s users on finance-related queries;
•	Managing the processes related to public monies transactions;
•	Serving as the point-of-contact between internal requestors and finance staff authorities;
•	Ensuring that finance processes/practices are in line with prevailing policies; 
•	Conducting sample finance audit checks and other internal controls to ensure proper governance; and
•	Reviewing and re-designing work processes to improve efficiency of processes

jobRequirements:
Requirements

•	Fields of studies in accountancy, business studies, finance or related field;
•	2-3 years of relevant experience in accounting or finance;
•	Proficiency in MS Office applications;
•	Able to work independently with minimum supervision;
•	Able to work under pressure with tight deadlines;
•	Have a good grasp of English Language and possess good communication and writing skills.

Short-listed candidates will be notified within two weeks after the closing date.

jobResponsibilities:
Your main responsibilities will be to provide administrative support in ensuring efficient management of daily tasks and scheduling of engagements for your principal. The key responsibilities include:  

a. Scheduling of meetings/events/engagements.  
b. Managing calendars, emails and phone calls;  
c. Making official work trip arrangements;  
d. Administrative support for the principal, and for the Division as assigned; 
e. Assist in organising events and/or related support work for the department 
f. Maintaining records and filing systems;  
g. Taking minutes of meetings; 
h. Managing budgets and expenditure; and 
i. Any other duties assigned by your principal.

jobRequirements:
Requirements: 
You should:
- be a quick learner, with a “can-do” attitude – able to operate in a fluid environment, pick up a wide spectrum of manpower issues, and never be shy of pushing the limits;  
• be able to appreciate and synthesise multiple perspectives from a myriad of stakeholders, across Government, industry, and the public.  
• be a self-starter and team player, with excellent communication, negotiation and project management skills;  
• dare to dream but with feet on the ground;  
• have prior or related experience in formulating public policies and running inter-agency projects; and  
• have strong analytical skills and be comfortable with numbers and basic econ-speak.

jobResponsibilities:
Specifically, you will: 

•	Develop and implement integrated communication strategies and create content that support METI’s announcements and initiatives; 
•	Design appropriate messaging to achieve the desired outcome of impactful and effective communication; 
•	Proactively develop media outreach and engagement strategies to profile and communicate the Ministry’s work; 
•	Collaborate with and manage external partners and agencies on media outreach and engagement; and 
•	Provide comms and staffing support for METI political office holders, including event assessments, drafting talking points and social media post(s), and handle media facilitation.

jobRequirements:
•	Relevant field of study in Communications, Public Relations, Arts and Social Sciences or relevant discipline; 
•	Minimum 1 to 2 years of related work experience in media relations or journalism preferred; applicants with no experience may apply;
•	Demonstrated ability in developing and implementing sound communications strategies and strong media relations skills; 
•	Good project management and organisational skills in a fast-paced environment; 
•	Strong writing skills; 
•	Interest in public sector policy matters and economy related issues; 
•	Able to negotiate and collaborate effectively at an advanced level.

jobResponsibilities:
TIER officers in the US Division are part of a dynamic and dedicated team responsible for advancing Singapore’s economic engagement with the United States. You will work on creative and innovative initiatives with colleagues in METI and our economic agencies that will develop your international economic perspectives, capabilities and experience by: 

•	Analysing and reporting on geostrategic developments and trends that affect the flows of goods, services, and investments; 

•	Formulating and refining strategies, policies and plans that enhance Singapore’s bilateral and plurilateral economic relations with the United States, often in consultation and coordination with other ministries and agencies across the Whole-of-Government; 

•	Networking and developing connections with foreign government and business counterparts; 

•	Preparing and executing communications, consultations and engagements with key stakeholders in the business community and general public; 

•	Organising and representing METI in visits, meetings, negotiations and conferences.

jobRequirements:
• Keen interest in international economic affairs and negotiations; 
• Strong analytical and conceptual abilities, with an eye for detail; 
• Excellent written and oral communication skills; 
• Self-starter, versatile and adaptable to different environments; 
• Ability to work well in teams and engage people; 
• Ability to work in a fast-paced and dynamic environment; and  
• Willingness to travel frequently

jobResponsibilities:
As an ITD officer, you will be assigned to one of four specialised teams covering trade in goods, digital economy and services, investment, or multilateral trade policy. You will deepen your knowledge, skills and expertise on a myriad of international trade issues and apply them in the following areas:

• Developing and implementing Singapore’s foreign economic policy;
• Representing Singapore in bilateral/multilateral trade and investment negotiations;
• Participating in international meetings and conferences;
• Providing advice to the Singapore Government on trade policy matters;
• Collaborating with external stakeholders, such as Singapore-based companies, business chambers and the general public;
• Ensuring Singapore’s full and timely implementation of international trade obligations; and
• Analysing international developments and their potential implications on Singapore

jobRequirements:
We are looking for candidates who are:
• Trained in Economics, Law, Political Science, International Relations, Accounting,
Business or related disciplines is preferred, but not essential;
• Keen interest in international economic affairs and negotiation;
• Strong analytical and conceptual abilities, with an eye for detail;
• Excellent written and oral communication skills;
• Ability to work well in teams and in a fast-paced and dynamic environment; and 
• Willingness to travel frequently

jobResponsibilities:
As a TIER officer in the Trade Strategy and Security Division, you will be part of a dynamic team working on fast-moving pieces to help Singapore navigate changes in our geo-economic environment. You will have the opportunity to hone your strategic thinking skillset, policy acumen, and international orientation perspectives in both the economic and security domains, by:

• Assessing the impact and implications of geo-political developments on Singapore’s economic and security interests;
• Developing strategies, policies, options and responses to expand Singapore’s economic heft or relevance as well as strengthen Singapore’s economic resilience;
• Preparing and executing communications and engagement strategies with key public and private sector stakeholders;
• Organising and representing METI at various high-level inter-agency platforms related to economic, security, and geo-political portfolios; and
• Collaborating and networking with various internal and external stakeholders

jobRequirements:
We are looking for dedicated team players who thrive in a fast-paced environment with:

• Relevant field of study in International Relations, Political Science, Public Policy,
Economics, Business, Finance, Accounting or any related discipline;
• Keen interest in the geo-political environment, as well as economic and security issues;
• Experience in policy formulation and data analysis;
• Excellent analytical, writing, communication, and presentation skills; and
• Strong project management and stakeholder management skills.

We are looking for someone who is curious about global and regional developments, enjoys engaging diverse stakeholders, and is motivated by the opportunity to contribute to policies and partnerships that strengthen Singapore's future. The successful candidate should also be committed to mentoring and developing officers, and to foster an inclusive and supportive team environment.

Some useful qualities include:
• Keen interest in North East Asian economies and regional developments;
• Excellent analytical and communication skills;
• Effectively bilingual in written and spoken English and Mandarin;
• Experience in public policy, economic policy, international relations, trade policy, investment promotion, or related fields;
• Experience in leading teams and managing stakeholder relationships; 
• Willingness to travel

agencyDescription:
The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is responsible for managing Singapore’s fiscal policies and the structure of its economy. We work to maintain international standards and best practices in areas such as company law, accounting standards, and corporate governance principles. We aim to advance the well-being and development of Singapore by:

•	achieving a balanced budget through prudent and sustainable fiscal policies;
•	ensuring the prudent investment of the government's reserves and other public funds;
•	setting out policies for government procurement, customs regulation, accounting standards and business regulation;
•	fostering a regulatory environment conducive to business and enterprise; and
•	ensuring that businesses operating within Singapore's jurisdiction are compatible with international standards and practices, in areas such as company law, accounting standards and corporate governance principles.

