jobResponsibilities:
Your primary responsibilities will broadly cover:
•	Formulating and reviewing candidate-related policies and legislation and devise plans to operationalise candidate-related policies and legislation. This includes working with other Government agencies on enforcement rules against illegal election campaigning, and contract management of ELD’s contractors for enforcement and audit works; 
•	Developing and reviewing communications materials for election candidates and their agents. This includes working with other Government agencies on publications such as advisories, guides, webpage contents and media releases;
•	Managing and enhancing digital services used by election candidates and their agents;
•	Engaging political parties and their representatives to raise awareness/educate them on new initiatives and electoral processes;
•	Serving as the first point of contact to political parties, election candidates and their agents. This includes responding to emails and calls, administering sales of electoral products and managing the political donations registry; and
•	Supporting election operations and other duties as assigned by supervisor or management, which may involve deployment across locations and working in a time-sensitive environment.

jobRequirements:
1.	Recognised Bachelor’s degree, preferably with relevant experience in organisational development, training, or learning and development;
2.	Strong ability to conceptualise, integrate, and execute training implementation plans, ensuring smooth and effective programme delivery;
3.	Experience in leading and co-ordinating large-scale training and learning projects involving multiple stakeholders;
4.	Skilled in analysing training evaluation data and identifying areas for improvement to enhance programme effectiveness; 
