jobResponsibilities:
NRF aims to develop interventions to nurture the pool of deep tech innovators that are critical in building a pipeline of deep tech unicorns.

The intern will deliver the following: 

(i) Review existing deep tech entrepreneurship programmes such as Activate and National GRIP, to assess whether they have been effective in helping deep tech entrepreneurs build successful spinoffs based on public research; 

(ii) Develop a life-cycle map of talent profiles required for deep tech startups, and identify critical gaps which may require interventions through an ecosystem map of initiatives as well as engagements with local startups and venture builders;

(iii) Perform a landscape scan of initiatives to train these identified talent profiles of deep tech talent;

(iv) Develop recommendations for NRF on possible interventions to nurture the identified profile(s) of deep tech talent.

This project will help the intern better appreciate the deep tech talent landscape in Singapore through engagements with key stakeholders such as startup founders and VBs, and offer the intern an opportunity to design an initiative that can address critical deep tech talent gaps.

