jobResponsibilities:
NRF aims to build research commercialisation partnerships with partners in global innovation hubs which can promote a two-way flow of Intellectual Property (IP) and talent. 

The intern will deliver the following: 

1. Help identify strong international partners that offer research commercialisation initiatives with a proven track record, and are embedded in vibrant innovation ecosystems. Identify the critical elements that the partner and their ecosystem can offer to accelerate research commercialisation in Singapore; 

2. Talk to key ecosystem stakeholders such as VCs, Venture Builders, corporates and government agencies to establish key value propositions for Singapore to attract top IP and talent here to commercialise their research;

3. Based on (1) and (2), design the operating model of the partnership that allows both Singapore and its international partner to achieve greater commercialisation outcomes through the partnership.

This project will help the intern better appreciate critical enablers required for successful deep tech hubs, the state of play of Singapore's own deep tech ecosystem, and offer the intern an opportunity to design an initiative that can strengthen our ecosystem.

